{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b0byumhjp","tool_use_id":"toolu_015EdqxSud5CDMzK2FqcvTwb","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run1-repo/41e8a498-9f0a-43c6-b233-527f1a246270/tasks/b0byumhjp.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_1_repair_1\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models\npython3 - \"$D\" <<'PY'\nimport sys,re\nD=sys.argv[1]\nsrc=open(\"individual_alternation_sensitivity_mirror.py\").read()\n# replace docstring\nend=src.index('\"\"\"',3)+3\ndoc='''\"\"\"Working-memory load: encoding noise grows with sequence length.\n\nPeople hold both sequences in working memory to compare them, and every extra\nflip adds encoding noise, so the same difference in apparent randomness decides\nthe choice less sharply for long sequences than for short ones (noise scales as\na power of the number of flips, a shared fitted exponent). The impression itself\nis the incumbent's: personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity, personal\nweights on heads/tails imbalance and the longest run, shared weights on the\nfinal run and on mirror symmetry, and a personal lapse rate.\n\"\"\"'''\nsrc=doc+src[end:]\nsrc=src.replace('        \"palin_b\": palindrome(b),\\n','        \"palin_b\": palindrome(b),\\n        \"log_len_rel\": float(np.log(len(a) / 5.0)),\\n',1)\nsrc=src.replace('    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\"','    log_len_rel = pm.Data(\"log_len_rel\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\"',1)\nsrc=src.replace('    # Personal lapse (guessing) rate.','''    # Shared memory-load exponent: encoding noise grows as (length / 5) ** eta,\n    # so positive eta means long pairs are compared less sharply.\n    eta = pm.Normal(\"eta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n\n    # Personal lapse (guessing) rate.''',1)\nsrc=src.replace('p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid(score_a - score_b)','p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid((score_a - score_b) * pt.exp(-eta * log_len_rel))',1)\nassert 'log_len_rel)' in src and '\"log_len_rel\": float' in src and 'eta = pm.Normal' in src\nopen(D+\"/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ngrep -n \"len(a)\\|a = \\|b = \" $D/candidate.py | head\ncat > $D/model_name.txt <<'EOF'\nlength_load_encoding_noise\nEOF\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md <<'EOF'\nRefinement of the incumbent `individual_alternation_sensitivity_mirror` by a working-memory load process: to compare two sequences people must hold both in memory, and every additional flip adds encoding noise, so the same difference in how random the two look decides the choice sharply for short sequences and only weakly for long ones (the noise grows as a power of the number of flips, by a shared fitted exponent that could also come out negative if longer sequences give more evidence). How random each sequence looks is still the incumbent's judgement — each person's own ideal switching rate and sensitivity to it, personal weights on heads/tails imbalance and the longest streak, shared weights on the final streak and mirror symmetry — and people still guess on some trials at a personal lapse rate.\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"557e5f14-4967-4abc-83d9-5efe909d071a","session_id":"41e8a498-9f0a-43c6-b233-527f1a246270"}
